APPLICATION CHECKLIST

1. Check source revisions, licenses and backups; stop any build using the target tree.
2. Run git apply --check, then git apply in each specified target repository, in the
   listed order; patch paths are relative to that repository, not the Android root.
3. Confirm the release configuration your build actually uses. The flag file is placed
   in the bp4a directory; a build that selects a different release configuration will
   not read it.
4. After flashing, verify on the device with
   adb shell aflags list | grep le_ase_read_multiple_variable
   which must report the flag as disabled, then connect the receiver over LE Audio.
5. Choose a sample rate or frame duration and confirm that the active stream
   configuration (dumpsys bluetooth_manager, "Stream config") follows it, with audible
   playback on the receivers you actually use.
